+# Full independent review request: 6600013
+
+Proposed outcome: scoped partials, original unsolved5/5. Please read every proof and verify the source/admissibility conditions independently of the finite controls. No sixth author search or publication before a full review.
+
+## Exact sources
+
+- quasicrystal_problems_2016.pdf: arXiv page8, Problem2.5.1 and its surrounding rational-versus-integral discussion; journal page587. The page was visually checked.
+- julien_2010.pdf: actually arXiv0804.0145v1,2008; its different numbering is explicit. Read Theorem5.10 and Proposition5.16, pp23–27, for the Rauzy proof, and the distinction between the known direction and the super-polynomial converse example. The source's published citation is Proposition6.7.
+- koivusalo_walton_2020.pdf: published ETDS41 (2021),1431–1463, online2020. Introduction, Example4.3 and Section8 distinguish canonical/quasicanonical from almost-canonical and explain the corrected topological identification. The packet does not invoke an unrestricted almost-canonical cohomology theorem.
+- julien_2017_homeomorphism.pdf: Section2 gives precise FLC, no-nonzero-period, repetitivity and translational-hull conventions.
+
+All four hashes are in SOURCE_MANIFEST.json. The PDFs are external research inputs and must not be uploaded with this packet.
+
+## Audit priorities
+
+Turn1: cofinal graph ranks versus persistent limit classes, the liminf slope bound, rational Künneth through finite graph products, exact box-complexity normalization and Sturmian sharpness.
+
+Turn2: legality and full aperiodicity of the sheared recoded product; exhaustive Thue–Morse recurrences; construction of the rectangular CW approximants and their inverse limit; signed Euler formula and why unbounded approximant ranks do not imply infinite hull rank.
+
+Turn3: the sup-inf stable-image formula and its quantifiers; exact cochain image rank formula; all collared graph adjacencies, unique substitution recognition and border reconstruction; homology versus cohomology transpose; actual class death rather than a false stability inference from finite data.
+
+Turn4: finite-stage covers versus arbitrary finite-to-one maps; fixed-radius flat transport and complexity bounds; independent cofinal choices of graph sizes; proper-substitution recognizability and growing borders; free-group inverse, lifted homotopy equivalences, connectedness and minimality of the covers; character calculation of(1,4,q+3).
+
+Turn5: the compatible2-adic cocycle, suspension/inverse-limit identification, genuine covering transfer and injective cohomology maps, nonexpansivity and failure of any finite continuous generator. Keep the infinite-rank profinite suspension outside the source until an admissible FLC generating model with one complexity constant is actually supplied. No such model is claimed.
+
+## Replay
+
+Run `python REPLAY_ALL.py`, optionally adding `--sources PATH`. All checkers use Python's standard library only. The third checker includes exact rational image-rank computations on the rectangular complexes through scale6; allow it to finish. Every receipt must match byte-for-byte. Final and historical manifests bind all frozen public author files.
+
+A passing verdict should remain scoped: the original arbitrary higher-dimensional implication is unresolved5/5. No novelty certification or blanket factor-map cohomology assertion is requested.
